markdown <<MARKDOWN
# The Shape of JSON

#### Before you write any code, you need to **see the shape** of the data.

---

## Scan the JSON

#### Don’t try to understand *everything* yet.
#### First, look for the **patterns**:

- ####  **Arrays**: ordered lists of items (look for **[ ]**)
- ####  **Objects**: key–value pairs (look for **{ }**)
- ####  **Values**: can be primitive (**string, number, boolean**) or nested inside objects/arrays

<div style="background-color:#B7E0E5; border-radius:10px; padding:14px; margin:18px auto; max-width:85%; box-sizing:border-box;">
  <p style="font-size:14pt; margin:0; line-height:130%;">💡 <strong>Tip:</strong> JSON isn’t random text. It has a structure. Your job is to spot the structure first.</p>
</div>

---

## JSON Sample 

<div style="background:#111; color:#f1f1f1; border-radius:12px; padding:16px; font-size:14pt; line-height:1.35; overflow:auto; max-height:520px; white-space:pre; border:1px solid #222;">
